	)
	(text "4-channel 4-20 mA input board for the Raspberry Pi 40-pin header - UNTESTED REFERENCE DESIGN\nEach channel: PTC -> field terminal (+) -> transmitter -> field terminal (-) -> 150 R shunt -> 0 V,\n  with TVS on both field wires, 4.7k/100n RC filter and BAT54S clamp in front of the ADS1115 input.\nADS1115 at 0x48 (ADDR = GND); move ADDR to VDD/SDA/SCL for 0x49/0x4A/0x4B to stack boards.\nOne external 24 V supply feeds all loops through J5; its 0 V is the Pi GND (non-isolated design).\nNot included: HAT+ ID EEPROM, mounting/keep-out, reverse-polarity protection, isolation,\n  GPIO-switchable 3.3 V rail for U1 (recommended for I2C recovery after a brown-out)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7af0bb65-2f37-5308-8ed7-3c08ffe9648f")
	)
